en:
For the torsion-free, metric-compatible connection, $\Gamma^r{}_{mn}
  =
  \frac12 g^{rs}
  \left(
    \partial_m g_{sn}
    +
    \partial_n g_{sm}
    -
    \partial_s g_{mn}
  \right).$ Thus normal coordinates satisfy $\Gamma^r{}_{mn}(p)=0.$

p.src:
The Levi–Civita connection also obeys metric compatibility: $\begin{aligned}
  \nabla_r g_{mn}
  &=
  \partial_r g_{mn}
  -
  \Gamma^s{}_{rm}g_{sn}
  -
  \Gamma^s{}_{rn}g_{ms}
  \nonumber\\
  &=0.
  \end{aligned}$ In normal coordinates at $p$, both $\partial g$ and $\Gamma$ vanish, so Eq.  is immediate there. Because $\nabla g$ is a tensor, its vanishing is then coordinate independent.

