p.src:
We now return to the part of the preceding lecture that curvature needs. Let a spatial curve be $x^m(s)$, with tangent $t^p=\frac{dx^p}{ds}.$ For a contravariant vector $v^m(s)$ defined along the curve, the covariant derivative along the curve is $\frac{D v^m}{Ds}
  =
  \frac{dv^m}{ds}
  +
  \Gamma^m{}_{np}v^n\frac{dx^p}{ds}.$ The ordinary derivative measures changes of both the vector and the local coordinate basis. The connection term removes the latter.

